Body:
This is exactly the workflow I was trying to describe: a backend, frontend, platform/infrastructure, and shared documentation repository need to be changed in one continuous OpenCode session while keeping each Git repository independent.

I opened #38984 before discovering these existing proposals. #19515 covers explicit workspace-folder access, and this issue covers the missing per-repository snapshot/undo semantics. I support the combined direction:

- explicitly selected additional repository roots rather than exposing an entire parent directory;
- independent Git status, diffs, branches, commits, and snapshots per root;
- one shared planning/context session across all selected repositories;
- per-root permission and configuration boundaries.

I will close #38984 as a duplicate so discussion and implementation details remain centralized here.

